    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm working at a repair shop here in Seoul and I just opened a high-end smartphone and the battery is visibly swollen. It's pushing against the screen. What are the immediate safety steps I need to take and how do I dispose of it properly? I need to know the standard SOP for this.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "**Immediate safety steps are crucial when dealing with a swollen battery, so you must stop working on the phone immediately.** Do not attempt to press down on the swelling, as this can cause a short circuit, and let the device sit in a safe, non-flammable area away from any flammable materials. You should carefully disconnect the battery connector *only* if you are absolutely certain of the procedure and have appropriate tools, but if you are unsure, leave it as is. For proper disposal, swollen lithium-ion batteries are considered hazardous waste; you must take them to a specialized e-waste recycling facility or a designated hazardous waste collection point in Seoul. Do not throw them in regular trash.",
